{"name":"Rustic Ranch","hex":"#8d794f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rustic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Country-styled or pastoral; rural.","Unfinished or roughly finished."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rural person.","An unsophisticated or uncultured person."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rustic"},{"term":"ranch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large plot of land used for raising cattle, sheep or other livestock.","A small farm that cultivates vegetables or livestock, especially one in the Southwestern United States."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To operate a ranch; to engage in ranching.","To work on a ranch."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ranch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ranch","blocks":[{"text":"A ranch is an area of land, including various structures, given primarily to ranching, the practice of raising grazing livestock such as cattle and sheep. It is a subtype of farm. These terms are most often applied to livestock-raising operations in Mexico, the Western United States and Western Canada, though there are ranches in other areas. People who own or operate a ranch are called ranchers, cattlemen, or stockgrowers. Ranching is also a method used to raise less common livestock such as horses, elk, American bison, ostrich, emu, and alpaca."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Grant-Kohrs_Ranch.jpg/330px-Grant-Kohrs_Ranch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranch","wikidata":"Q509028"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Sennudem_001.jpg/500px-Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Sennudem_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Sennudem_001.jpg/1280px-Maler_der_Grabkammer_